{"answer":"Yes — den is built for exactly this. A custom class in den is a *forwarding* class: `den.batteries.forward` collects each aspect's `myconf` content and injects it as ordinary Nix modules into a target class's module tree. Merging is then just NixOS module-system merge semantics (list concatenation, `mkForce`, …), and "evaluated per host" happens automatically when the host is instantiated.

Verified against `sini/den` (fork of `denful/den`) on `main`:

**1. Define the class (`modules/aspects/batteries/forward.nix`, impl `nix/lib/forward.nix`)**

```nix
# modules/myconf.nix
{ den, lib, ... }:
let
  # myconf contents -> the host's nixos class, per host
  myconf-to-nixos =
    { class, aspect-chain }:
    den.batteries.forward {
      each = lib.singleton class;
      fromClass = _: "myconf";
      intoClass = _: "nixos";
      intoPath  = _: [ ];      # [] = merge at the class root
      fromAspect = _: lib.head aspect-chain;
    };
in {
  den.classes.myconf = { };    # register the name so aspect keys dispatch (same pattern
                               # flake.nix uses for the packages/apps/checks classes)
  den.schema.host.includes = [ myconf-to-nixos ];  # every host
}
```

Then aspects just set `myconf` content and the pieces merge like a NixOS module tree:

```nix
den.aspects.foo = { myconf = { items = [ "from-foo" ]; }; };
den.aspects.bar = { myconf.items = [ "from-bar" ]; };
```

If you want typed options for the tree, declare the option on the target and forward into a subpath — exactly what den's own test does (`templates/ci/modules/public-api/forward-from-custom-class.nix`, `test-forward-into-subpath`): the nixos side declares `options.fwd-box = lib.mkOption { type = lib.types.submoduleWith { modules = [ ... ]; }; }`, the custom `src` class forwards with `intoPath = _: [ "fwd-box" ]`, and the lists from both sides merge into one.

**2. Flake output (`modules/policies/flake.nix`, `modules/outputs.nix`)**

- Per-host result: nothing to do. `system-to-os-outputs` resolves every `den.hosts.<system>.<name>`, calls `policy.instantiate host` (which runs `nixosSystem` over the merged module tree, your `myconf` content included) and lands it at `flake.nixosConfigurations.<name>`. Override `intoAttr` per host for other paths (`docs/.../reference/output.mdx`).
- Standalone flake output: route the class into the `flake` class, the same way the built-in `packages-to-flake` policy does:

```nix
den.policies.myconf-to-packages =
  { system, ... }:
  [ (den.lib.policy.route {
      fromClass = "myconf";
      intoClass = "flake";
      path = [ "flake" "packages" system "myconf" ];
    }) ];
den.schema.flake-system.includes = [ den.policies.myconf-to-packages ];
```

- Merge semantics: when *several aspects* write the same flake output attribute, import the option definition so the module system knows how to merge: `imports = [ inputs.den.flakeOutputs.packages ]` (also `.nixosConfigurations`, `.homeConfigurations`, `.flake`, `.all` — see `nix/flakeOutputs.nix`). Regression test `templates/ci/modules/public-api/packages-merge.nix` (den #572) shows two aspects defining `packages` both appearing in `config.flake.packages.<system>`, and overlapping keys erroring with "den: the option `shared' has conflicting definitions from multiple aspects".

The docs' `files` → `flake-parts` example in `docs/src/content/docs/guides/custom-classes.mdx` is the same pattern end-to-end: `den.classes.files = { }` + a `den.lib.policy.route` policy + `den.schema.flake-parts.includes = [...]`.

How I know: read `modules/aspects/batteries/forward.nix` (battery = `den.lib.forward.forwardEach`), `nix/lib/forward.nix` (how content is injected as modules with `guard`/`adaptArgs`/`intoPath`), `modules/policies/flake.nix` (class registration + the `*to-flake` route policies + per-host `instantiate`), `nix/flakeOutputs.nix` (merge-semantics options), `nix/default.nix` (exports `flakeOutputs`, `lib`, `templates`), plus the two cited doc pages and the two public-api test files.

Caveat: I could not run a live `eval` in this environment (clone/eval were unavailable here), so this is source-verified at `main`, not evaluated at your rev — if your den input is pinned to an older rev, the `policy.route`/`deliver` API (a permanent sugar shim) is what to check for first.","confidence":0.82,"gaps":["No eval was run: the recipe was verified by reading sini/den source on main (forward.nix, nix/lib/forward.nix, modules/policies/flake.nix, nix/flakeOutputs.nix, packages-merge.nix, custom-classes/output docs), not evaluated at the asker's pinned den rev","Exact sha of sini/den main not pinned (page shows 641 commits, no rev hash); asker's input rev may differ","den.provides.forward (used in templates/ci tests) vs den.batteries.forward (used in docs): only den.batteries.forward's definition was read; the den.provides alias definition was not","The aspect-key dispatch code that reads den.classes was not read directly; the registration pattern is corroborated by two independent usages (flake.nix system-output classes, docs files-class example)"],"escalate_forced":"no"}

