{"answer":"**Yes** — this is exactly what den's library mode is for, and den ships a template that does precisely this: no hosts, only aspects setting a custom class, resolved and evaluated outside den.

## The API

`den.lib.aspects.resolve "<class>" <aspect>` collects all module content for that class out of an aspect tree and returns **`{ imports = [ ... ]; }`** — a plain module you can feed to any module system. Verified in `denful/den@main`, `nix/lib/aspects/fx/resolve.nix`:

```nix
# Back-compatible projection: imports only. Protects deferredModule consumers
# that assert resolve's output is exactly { imports = …; }.
fxResolve = mkPipeline: args: { inherit (fxResolveFull mkPipeline args) imports; };
```

So: `lib.evalModules { modules = [ module your-base-module; ]; }` (or nvf / terranix / whatever you have) — den only *collects*, you evaluate.

## Working example with zero hosts

The `nvf-standalone` template (`templates/nvf-standalone/modules/`) declares **no hosts and no users** — just aspects setting a custom `vim` class, forwarded into an `nvf` class, then resolved by the user's own module system (`nvf-integration.nix`):

```nix
den.lib.nvf.module = vimAspect: ctx:
let
  vimClass =
    { class, aspect-chain }:
    den.batteries.forward {
      each = lib.singleton true;
      fromClass = _: "vim";
      intoClass = _: "nvf";
      intoPath = _: [ "vim" ];
      fromAspect = _: lib.head aspect-chain;
      adaptArgs = lib.id;
    };
  aspect = den.lib.parametric.fixedTo ctx {
    includes = [ vimClass vimAspect ];
  };
in den.lib.aspects.resolve "nvf" aspect;   # → { imports = [...]; }
```

The result goes into `inputs.nvf.lib.neovimConfiguration { modules = [ ... ] }` — the user's own evaluation — and the whole thing runs with `nix run .#my-neovim` (template `flake.nix` just imports `inputs.den.flakeModule` + `flakeOutputs.packages`).

## Docs confirmation

The "Library vs Framework" page (den.denful.dev/explanation/library-vs-framework) states it directly:

- *"Den's core (`nix/default.nix`) is domain-agnostic… Nothing here assumes NixOS, Darwin, or Home Manager."*
- *"Library only: You have a custom Nix module system (Terranix, NixVim, system-manager) and want parametric aspect dispatch without Den's host/user/home framework."*
- Non-OS-domain example:

```nix
den.aspects.web-server = {
  terranix.resource.aws_instance.web.ami = "...";
  includes = [ ({ env, ... }: { terranix.resource.aws_instance.web.tags.Env = env; }) ];
};
# Resolve for your custom "terranix" class.
module = den.lib.aspects.resolve "terranix" den.aspects.web-server;
```

## Notes for your case

- If your custom class is a **top-level class** (not forwarding into another class), you can skip the `den.batteries.forward` battery entirely: your aspect just sets `myClass = ...`, and `den.lib.aspects.resolve "myClass" aspect` collects it directly.
- `den.lib.aspects.resolveImports` is a variant that skips entity instantiation (phases 1–3 only) — useful for nested extraction (e.g. pulling a homeManager module out of a host tree).
- The template's `den.lib.parametric.fixedTo` (used to pin context) is **deprecated** — the docs say the pipeline now dispatches bare functions in `includes` automatically, so you can drop it.
- Den's core is zero-dependency, so you can import it as a plain Nix library (`import (fetchTarball "github:denful/den") { inherit lib; }` or a flake input) and use `den.lib` without any of the flake/schema machinery.

Caveat: I could not run `eval` in this session (the tool was unavailable), so the claims above rest on reading the raw source files at `denful/den@main` (`nix/default.nix`, `nix/lib/aspects/default.nix`, `nix/lib/aspects/fx/resolve.nix`, `templates/nvf-standalone/modules/{den,nvf-integration}.nix`) plus the docs pages, not on an evaluated value. If your aspect is a parametric function that needs specific context values, the ctx-pinning detail is the one place to double-check against your own aspect.","confidence":0.8,"gaps":["did not evaluate den.lib.aspects.resolve at denful/den@main (eval unavailable in this session); verified by reading nix/lib/aspects/fx/resolve.nix and the docs page","did not check the asker's own aspect/class shape — if their aspect is a context-dependent function, ctx handling (deprecated fixedTo vs. automatic dispatch) needs checking against their code","did not verify denful/den main is the rev the asker uses; citations are from main as of now"],"escalate_forced":"no"}

