{"answer":"**Keep the host's `nixpkgs` input on stable, and pull the few unstable packages from a second, pinned `nixpkgs-unstable` input.** Don't switch the host's main `nixpkgs` — in den, every class module's `pkgs` comes from it, so that one input is what keeps the system stable.

How this fits den (checked in `sini/den` @ `main`):

- The `nixos` class is instantiated by `inputs.nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem` by default, and den documents exactly this escape hatch in the host schema (`nix/lib/entities/host.nix`, option `den.schema.host.instantiate`): *"Set explicitly if you need: a custom input name, eg, nixos-unstable"*.
- `inputs` is available in every module as a special arg (`specialArgs.inputs = inputs` — see the *From Zero to Den* guide), so an aspect can reach any flake input alongside `pkgs`.

So the recommended pattern:

```nix
# flake.nix
inputs.nixpkgs.url = "github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixpkgs-25.05";        # stable — everything else
inputs.nixpkgs-unstable.url = "github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixpkgs-unstable";
```

```nix
# in your aspect (flat-form class module)
den.aspects.laptop = {
  nixos = { inputs, pkgs, ... }: {
    environment.systemPackages =
      with pkgs; [
        firefox              # stable, from the host's pkgs
      ] ++ [
        (inputs.nixpkgs-unstable.legacyPackages.${pkgs.system}.my-unstable-tool)
      ];
  };
};
```

