- **Footgun to avoid:** if you instead write the whole aspect parametric at host scope — `den.aspects.my-feature = { host, user }: lib.optionalAttrs (...) { homeManager = ...; }` included from a host — the aspect fans out per user but emits class-locally **on the host**, "where homeManager is inert", so the content never reaches the users' Home Manager evaluation (`docs/src/content/docs/guides/home-manager.mdx`, "Host-scope parametric aspects no longer deliver homeManager content to users"). That's why the activation belongs on the user side (`den.schema.user.includes` / `den.aspects.<user>.includes`).

