{"answer":"Two parts: den already gives you the `nixosConfigurations` half for free, and the `deploy.nodes` half is a den `flake`-class aspect.

## 1. Top-level `nixosConfigurations` from your den hosts

Den instantiates every entry in `den.hosts` into `flake.nixosConfigurations.<name>` by default (no extra setup; `intoAttr` overrides where it lands). To surface the whole flake from your `flake.nix`:

```nix
# flake.nix
{
  inputs.nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixpkgs-unstable";
  inputs.import-tree.url = "github:denful/import-tree";
  inputs.den.url = "github:denful/den";

  outputs = inputs:
    let
      den = (inputs.nixpkgs.lib.evalModules {
        modules = [ (inputs.import-tree ./modules) ];
        specialArgs.inputs = inputs;
      }).config;
    in
    {
      inherit (den.flake) nixosConfigurations;  # add `deploy` (below)
    };
}
```

Den defines its own `options.flake` (in `nix/flakeOutputs.nix`) so this works with or without flake-parts; if you *do* use flake-parts, add `inputs.den.flakeOutputs.flake` to that `modules` list so flake-parts' `flake` option is what den writes. If everything is defined den-side, `outputs` can simply be `... .config.flake`.

## 2. `deploy.nodes` per host

`deploy` is a top-level (not system-keyed) flake attribute, which is exactly what den's non-per-system **`flake` class** is for. One caveat from the docs: the `flake` class only merges **one level deep** — two aspects writing `flake.deploy.nodes.a` and `flake.deploy.nodes.b` don't merge, the second `nodes` replaces the first silently. So build the whole attribute in **one place** from `den.hosts`:

```nix
# modules/deploy.nix
{ den, lib, ... }:
{
  den.aspects.deploy = {
    flake.flake.deploy.nodes =
      lib.mapAttrs (name: _: {
        host = "root@${name}";            # your deploy-rs target per host
        # deploy.path = "/var/nix-deploy";  # optional
      }) den.hosts.x86_64-linux;
  };

  den.schema.flake.includes = [ den.aspects.deploy ];  # flake class lives at the flake root
}
```

Then `inherit (den.flake) nixosConfigurations deploy;` in `flake.nix`. If you have hosts on several systems, do the `lib.mapAttrs` per `den.hosts.<system>` and merge the results in that one place.

