`clone` and `eval` were unavailable in this session, so I verified against the repo's own documentation, not an eval: I fetched `https://github.com/sini/gen-merge` (README, main) and `flake.nix` from raw.githubusercontent.com at main (latest commit `03f17a6`, Oct 16 2026 per the commits page). All claims above are quoted from the README sections I read (Usage, "The 7-item merge primitive", "The priority subset", "The nixpkgs optionType protocol", "Redeclaring an option", "Known byte-mode boundaries") and from the flake's `outputs.lib` wiring.

