```nix
den.default.includes = [ den.batteries.inputs' ];   # all hosts/users/homes
# or scoped to one aspect:
den.aspects.laptop.includes = [ den.batteries.inputs' ];
```

The battery injects `_module.args.inputs' = inputs'` into every class module it is included for (`modules/aspects/batteries/flake-parts/inputs.nix`), so your NixOS module functions can simply be:

```nix
den.aspects.laptop.nixos = { inputs', pkgs, ... }: {
  environment.systemPackages = [ inputs'.my-flake.packages.my-pkg ];
};
```

`inputs'` is the flake's `inputs` with the system pre-selected, so modules don't need `pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.system`. Requires flake-parts (den's default template uses it).

**2. True `specialArgs` via the host's `instantiate` option — for any value, under any name**

Host entities have an `instantiate` option (`nix/lib/entities/host.nix`), whose description says: *"Set explicitly if you need: … adding specialArgs when absolutely required."* Den invokes it as `instantiate { modules = …; }` (`applyInstantiates` in `nix/lib/aspects/fx/resolve.nix` — args are `{ modules }`, plus `pkgs` when the spec defines one, plus a `nixpkgs.hostPlatform` module when the host sets `system`), so the wrapper is:

```nix
{ inputs, ... }:
{
  den.hosts.laptop.instantiate = { modules, ... }:
    inputs.nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
      inherit modules;
      specialArgs = { inherit inputs; };
    };
};
```

Now every NixOS module for that host can pattern-match `{ inputs, pkgs, ... }` — literal `specialArgs` semantics, and it's also how you'd swap to a custom input name (e.g. `nixos-unstable`). The same `instantiate` option exists on `den.homes.<name>` for homeManager (use `extraSpecialArgs` there).

