{"answer":"Two mechanisms do this in NixOS, both built into the module system (checked against `NixOS/nixpkgs` @ master, Oct 2026):

## 1. A specialisation — the idiomatic "same host, only the driver differs" variant

The specialisation module exists for exactly this: *"They are only (directly) accessible when the parent configuration is boot default… you can provide an easy way to boot the same configuration as you use, but with another kernel"* (`nixos/modules/system/activation/specialisation.nix`).

```nix
# your host module / flake
{
  # ...your normal config (e.g. nvidia driver) ...

  specialisation = {                 # current nixpkgs (2026); older releases: system.specialisations
    amdgpu = {
      inheritParentConfig = true;    # default: inherit the whole host config
      configuration = {
        # only the diff
        hardware.nvidia.enable = false;
        hardware.amd_gpu.enable = true;
        system.nixos.tags = [ "amdgpu" ];   # appears in the menu label
      };
    };
  };
}
```

- `nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#host` — or `nixos-rebuild boot` to install the entries without switching the running system, then reboot and pick.
- **GRUB**: the current generation becomes a submenu — "NixOS – Default" (your normal config) plus one entry per specialisation (`addGeneration` in `install-grub.pl` reads each specialisation's `configuration-name`/`nixos-version` for the entry name). **systemd-boot**: "NixOS (amdgpu)" next to "NixOS" (title built in `systemd-boot-builder.py`).
- No new generation is created: the variant follows your current generation (and only exists while that generation is the default one — that's in the module's comment).
- You can also flip to it at runtime, no reboot: `sudo /run/current-system/specialisation/amdgpu/bin/switch-to-configuration switch` (from the option's own docs).
- Driver note: fine as long as the driver loads at stage 2 (the usual amdgpu/nvidia case). Each specialisation is a full child toplevel with its own `kernel-params`/`init`, so kernel-parameter changes apply too.

## 2. A full separate configuration — a persistent, independent boot entry

Define a second `nixosConfigurations` for the same machine (shared module file, driver diff only):

```nix
# flake.nix
outputs = { self, nixpkgs }: {
  nixosConfigurations.laptop = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
    modules = [ ./hosts/laptop/default.nix ];
  };
  nixosConfigurations.laptop-amdgpu = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
    modules = [ ./hosts/laptop/default.nix { /* driver diff */ } ];
  };
};
```

- `nixos-rebuild boot --flake .#laptop-amdgpu` installs it as a **generation** without switching; reboot and pick it. Use `switch` to make it the default.
- GRUB lists all generations under the "NixOS – All configurations" submenu (`addProfile` in `install-grub.pl`); systemd-boot lists them as entries. Both cap the count: `boot.loader.grub.configurationLimit` (default 100 in current nixpkgs) and `boot.loader.systemd-boot.configurationLimit` (see NixOS wiki "Bootloader").
- To make the entries distinguishable, set `system.nixos.tags = [ "amdgpu" ];` (or `system.nixos.label`) in that configuration — that string lands in the `nixos-version`/bootspec label both bootloaders display (`nixos/modules/misc/label.nix`, `activation/bootspec.nix`).
- Variant: install under a named profile (`nixos-rebuild --profile /nix/var/nix/profiles/system-profiles/amdgpu ...`) — GRUB then shows a dedicated "NixOS – Profile 'amdgpu'" submenu.

**Which to pick:** specialisation for a driver toggle (light, follows the current generation); a separate configuration/profile when the variant needs its own kernel/initrd/package set and a stable, independent entry. Same options are available in den, since den composes the same NixOS module system.","confidence":0.8,"gaps":["Option name drift: current master defines `specialisation` (activation/specialisation.nix); I did not verify the rename/alias history for the older `system.specialisations` name users on older releases would have.","Did not read systemd-boot.nix to confirm the exact `configurationLimit` option name/default (wiki + builder placeholder @configurationLimit@ were checked).","Example driver options (hardware.nvidia.enable, hardware.amd_gpu.enable) were not verified against the asker's nixpkgs version.","No repo/rev was provided, so no eval of the asker's actual configuration was run.","Den-specific statement (options available in den) is inference, not verified from den source."],"escalate_forced":"no"}

