{"answer":"Use nixpkgs' per-package whitelist instead of the global switch:

```nix
{
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfreePackages = [ "steam" "nvidia-x11" ];
}
```

This is a list of package names (matched against the package's `pname`). Any unfree package not in the list still fails the unfree-license check at eval time; the listed ones are allowed. Put it at the top level of your NixOS module / flake config — it applies to the whole nixpkgs instance, so it covers `environment.systemPackages`, `services.xserver.videoDrivers = [ "nvidia" ]`, etc.

```nix
{
  ...
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfreePackages = [ "steam" "nvidia-x11" ];

  environment.systemPackages = [ pkgs.steam ];
  services.xserver.videoDrivers = [ "nvidia" ];
}
```

Caveats:

- The license check runs for every package that is *evaluated*, including dependencies. `steam` depends on `steam-original` (prebuilt binaries from Valve), which has its own unfree license — if you get a new "license is not free" error naming it, add `"steam-original"` to the list too. The error message names the exact package to whitelist.
- `nvidia-x11` may not trigger the unfree check at all (the NixOS nvidia driver has historically built without any `allowUnfree*` setting); listing it is harmless, you can drop it if it's never in an error.

