{"answer":"The option is **`nix.settings.trusted-users`** — it maps directly to `trusted-users` in `/etc/nix/nix.conf`. The warning is emitted because you (a user not in that list) are using a substituter that is not in `trusted-substituters`; Nix then ignores that substituter for you.

```nix
{
  nix.settings.trusted-users = [ "root" "your-user" ];
}
```

Then `nixos-rebuild switch` (or `switch-to-configuration`). Your user then has full daemon rights, which includes being able to use any substituter, so the warning goes away. Note the module sets the default to `[ "root" ]` and a user-set value *replaces* it, so keep `"root"` in the list (root bypasses the daemon anyway on NixOS).

If you don't want to make the whole user trusted and only want a specific cache trusted, use the narrower option instead:

```nix
nix.settings.trusted-substituters = [ "https://your-cache.example.org/" ];
