{"answer":"Two steps: make the host's users Home Manager users, then deliver the shared options from the **host's aspect** via `provides.to-users`.

**1. Give the users on that host the `homeManager` class** (user `classes` default to `[ "user" ]` only, so Home Manager is opt-in):

```nix
den.hosts.x86_64-linux.igloo = {
  users.tux.classes   = [ "homeManager" ];
  users.alice.classes = [ "homeManager" ];
  # ... one entry per user on igloo
};
```

That's all the enabling: the `home-manager` battery (`modules/aspects/batteries/home-manager.nix`, built by `makeHomeEnv` in `nix/lib/home-env.nix`) auto-sets `home-manager.enable` when the host has at least one user with the class, imports the Home Manager OS module into the host, and forwards each such user's `homeManager` class content into `home-manager.users.<userName>` (`forwardPathFn = { user, ... }: [ "home-manager" "users" user.userName ]`).

**2. Put the options that should hit *every* user on igloo in the host aspect's `provides.to-users`:**

```nix
# den auto-creates an aspect named after each host, so `den.aspects.igloo` is
# the host's own aspect.
den.aspects.igloo = {
  # delivered to ALL users on igloo
  provides.to-users = { user, ... }: {
    homeManager.home.stateVersion = "24.11";
    homeManager.programs.helix.enable = true;
  };

  # optional: target a single user by name instead
  provides.alice.homeManager.programs.vim.enable = true;
};
```

Per-user config then stays in the user aspect as usual (`den.aspects.tux.homeManager = { ... }`).

**How I know:** this is documented in den's guides — `docs/src/content/docs/guides/mutual.mdx` ("Configuring peers from the host": `provides` registered on the *host* aspect, whose subtree spans every user on it; on a user aspect it's subtree-scoped and never reaches sibling users) and `docs/src/content/docs/guides/home-manager.mdx` (enabling, forwarding into `home-manager.users.<name>`), backed by the source above.

